 4. 📸 Pic du jour 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A replica of President Trump's Oval Office is updated to the current decor by workers at The People's House exhibition in D.C. Photo: J. Scott Applewhite/AP The White House Historical Association's People's House exhibition near the White House has overhauled its replica Oval Office for visitors to experience President Trump's second-term design choices.

 It's glitzier. And there's way more gold, AP reports. The same rococo flourishes Trump installed in the world's most famous workspace have been recreated down to each wall appliqué at the White House Historical Association's replica Oval Office, which opened in September 2024.

 Gleaming vases, golden-hued swirling onlays, two dozen portraits in heavy gilded frames and knickknacks crowding nearly every available surface. Keep reading . 

 
 
